# My Greetings!

I rejoice to see the *Inamuzhakkam* Pongal annual appear.

Comrade Chitrarasu has long been known to the country in the world of letters. Its publisher, Comrade Kannappa Valliyappan, is a worthy and youthful man of movement enthusiasm, born into a prosperous family.

The editor's fiery writing and the publisher's youthful vitality are highly compatible.

Countless journals arise in our movement day by day. Yet young people and students eager to read them all continue to arise alongside them. To say our literary camp keeps growing and expanding is to proclaim forcefully that these are the bounds of Dravidam. I am proud that *Inamuzhakkam* possesses the ability to stand in the front rank of that great army of warriors.

Long live *Inamuzhakkam*.

Affectionately,

Annadurai

(14 January 1960; *Inamuzhakkam* Pongal Annual)
